2654 0 obj<</Border[0 0 0]/Contents(9)/F 64/Rect[1370 740 1382 749]/Subtype/Square/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/NM(XNBIOWDIPFUSMUVW)/M(D:20260811142352-07'00')/AP<</N 1835 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>9</p></body>)>>
endobj
2655 0 obj<</Border[0 0 0]/Contents(ELECTRICAL ROOM LOCATION. FIELD VERIFY PANEL LOCATIONS PRIOR TO INSTALLATION. ALL EXISTING ELECTRICAL DEVICES IN THIS AREA AND NOT PART OF THIS SCOPE OF WORK TO REMAIN. ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR TO MAINTAIN THE CONTINUITY OF EXISTING ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR TO MAINTAIN THE CONTINUITY OF EXISTING BRANCH CIRCUIT WIRING. EACH GENERAL USE MULTIWIRE BRANCH CIRCUIT SHALL BE PROVIDED WITH A MEANS THAT WILL SIMULTANEOUSLY DISCONNECT ALL UNGROUNDED CONDUCTORS AT THE POINT OF DISTRIBUTION. PER 240.15B\(1\), INDIVIDUAL SINGLE POLE CIRCUIT BREAKERS WITH IDENTIFIED HANDLE TIES, SHALL BE PERMITTED AS THE PROTECTION FOR EACH UNGROUNDED CONDUCTOR FOR MULTIWIRE BRANCH CIRCUITS THAT SERVE ONLY SINGLE PHASE TO NEUTRAL LOADS. PROVIDE SEPARATE GROUND AND SEPARATE NEUTRAL FOR ALL A/V, IT, AND LIGHTING CIRCUITS. FINAL CONNECTION TO FURNITURE SYSTEM SHALL BE COORDINATED WITH FURNITURE SYSTEM INSTALLER. FURNITURE SYSTEM FEED SHALL BE A 2+2, 8-WIRE SYSTEM CONSISTING OF 4#12 HOT \(H\), 2#12 NEUTRAL \(N\), & 2#12 EQUIPMENT GROUND \(EG\) IN 3/4" CONDUIT. PROVIDE LEGRAND WIREMOLD 4" FIRE RATED FURNITURE FEED POKE-THRU DEVICE WITH 3/4"C FOR POWER, 44FATC15 OR EQUIVALENT. VERIFY WITH FURNITURE VENDOR AND ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ORDERING AND ROUGH-IN. CONFIRM FINISH WITH ARCHITECT AND DATA REQUIREMENTS WITH IT DRAWINGS. REFER TO ELECTRICAL DETAIL SHEET FOR TYPICAL FURNITURE SYSTEM LAYOUT AND FURNITURE FEED. VERIFY EQUIPMENT POWER CONNECTIONS WITH ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ORDERING/ROUGH-IN. ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR SHALL COORDINATE WITH FIRE ALARM SYSTEM TO SHUT DOWN AV SOUND SYSTEM WITH ASSOCIATED OUTLETS IN ENCLOSED ROOMS WHEN FIRE ALARM SYSTEM IS ACTIVATED, AS REQUIRED. AV CONTRACTOR TO PROVIDE RELAY INTEGRATED POWER DISTRIBUTION DEVICE FURMAN CN-15MP MINIPORT OR EQUIVALENT.  PROVIDE 6" POKE-THROUGH DEVICE LEGRAND WIREMOLD 6AT OR EQUIVALENT TO SERVE POWER AND DATA. REFER TO AV/IT PLANS FOR FURTHER AV EQUIPMENT SPECIFICATIONS. VERIFY WITH ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ORDERING/ROUGH-IN. PROVIDE 8" POKE-THROUGH DEVICE LEGRAND WIREMOLD 8AT OR EQUIVALENT TO SERVE POWER, DATA AND HDMI. REFER TO AV/IT PLANS FOR FURTHER AV EQUIPMENT SPECIFICATIONS. VERIFY WITH ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ORDERING/ROUGH-IN. PROVIDE 1" CONDUIT ONLY WITH PULL WIRE AND REQUIRED BACK BOX STUB UP TO CEILING SPACE OR PLENUM FOR CARD READER. COORDINATE WITH SECURITY AND/OR AV/IT CONSULTANT PRIOR TO ROUGH-IN. REFER TO AV/IT DRAWINGS FOR ALL REQUIRED CARD READER LOCATIONS. PROVIDE 120V CIRCUIT FOR ELEVATOR SMOKE CURTAIN, SMOKE GUARD SYSTEM MODEL   200400OR EQUIVALENT. PROVIDE CONTROL AS REQUIRED FOR WORKABLE SYSTEM. ALL 120 VOLT, SINGLE PHASE, 15-20 AMP RECEPTACLES INSTALLED WITHIN 6' OF ANY POINT ALONG THE OUTSIDE EDGE OF A SINK SHALL BE GFCI PROTECTED. FOR RECEPTACLES NOT ACCESSIBLE, GFCI CIRCUIT BREAKER TO BE PROVIDED. NOT USED. NOT USED. VERIFY ROOM POWER REQUIREMENTS WITH AV/IT CONSULTANT PRIOR TO ROUGH-IN. PROVIDE AND INSTALL RATED DISCONNECT SWITCH AND AS REQUIRED FOR CONNECTIONS TO ELECTRIC WATER HEATER LOCATED PER PLUMBING DRAWINGS. LOCATE AND INSTALL DISCONNECT SWITCH ADJACENT TO ELECTRIC WATER HEATER AND COORDINATE EXACT REQUIREMENTS TO PLUMBING CONTRACTOR BEFORE ROUGH-IN. 120V RECEPTACLES IN OFFICES, LOBBIES, CONFERENCE ROOMS, PANTRIES, AND COPY ROOMS SHALL BE CONTROLLED AND AUTOMATICALLY TURN OFF WITH THE LIGHTS PER TITLE 24. A CONTROLLED RECEPTACLE DISTINCTLY LABELED SHALL BE LOCATED WITHIN 6' OF EACH UNCONTROLLED RECEPTACLE. PROVIDE SPLIT CIRCUITING RECEPTACLES, HALF CONTROLLED AND HALF UNCONTROLLED, WHERE REQUIRED. ROUTE EACH CONTROLLED RECEPTACLE CIRCUIT THROUGH A RELAY. TIE RELAY TO LOCAL CONTROL UNIT AND OCCUPANCY SENSOR. REFER TO WIRING DIAGRAM ON SHEET E032. FURROUT WALL 6" TO ALLOW FOR RECESSED INSTALLATION OF PANEL. CONFIRM AND COORDINATE FINAL PANEL INSTALL LOCATION WITH ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ORDERING/ROUGH-IN. PROVIDE HARDWIRED CONNECTION TO ALL PHONE BOOTHS. VERIFY WITH ARCHITECT AND FURNITURE VENDOR THE PHONE BOOTH POWER REQUIREMENTS PRIOR TO ORDERING AND ROUGH-IN. PER AV DRAWINGS, PROVIDE 1-1/4" CONDUIT TO NEAREST ACCESSIBLE CEILING FOR AV, 1" CONDUIT TO NEAREST ACCESSIBLE CEILING FOR DATA. REFER TO AV DRAWINGS FOR FURTHER INFORMATION AND EXACT REQUIREMENTS. PROVIDE 4" POKE-THROUGH DEVICE LEGRAND WIREMOLD 4AT OR EQUIVALENT TO SERVE POWER. VERIFY WITH ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ORDERING/ROUGH-IN. PROVIDE LEGRAND CONNECTRAC EXPRESS KIT FOR 1-CIRCUIT POWER CONNECTION TO SERVE EQUIPMENT. VERIFY WITH ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ORDERING/ROUGH-IN. COORDINATE ALL CONNECTIONS WITH FURNITURE VENDOR PRIOR TO ORDERING/ROUGH-IN.)/F 64/Rect[764 322 1804 732]/Subtype/Square/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/NM(KUYPBJHCWBYFBWAU)/M(D:20260811142352-07'00')/AP<</N 1836 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>ELECTRICAL ROOM LOCATION. FIELD VERIFY PANEL LOCATIONS PRIOR TO INSTALLATION. ALL EXISTING ELECTRICAL DEVICES IN THIS AREA AND NOT PART OF THIS SCOPE OF WORK TO REMAIN. ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR TO MAINTAIN THE CONTINUITY OF EXISTING ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR TO MAINTAIN THE CONTINUITY OF EXISTING BRANCH CIRCUIT WIRING. EACH GENERAL USE MULTIWIRE BRANCH CIRCUIT SHALL BE PROVIDED WITH A MEANS THAT WILL SIMULTANEOUSLY DISCONNECT ALL UNGROUNDED CONDUCTORS AT THE POINT OF DISTRIBUTION. PER 240.15B\(1\), INDIVIDUAL SINGLE POLE CIRCUIT BREAKERS WITH IDENTIFIED HANDLE TIES, SHALL BE PERMITTED AS THE PROTECTION FOR EACH UNGROUNDED CONDUCTOR FOR MULTIWIRE BRANCH CIRCUITS THAT SERVE ONLY SINGLE PHASE TO NEUTRAL LOADS. PROVIDE SEPARATE GROUND AND SEPARATE NEUTRAL FOR ALL A/V, IT, AND LIGHTING CIRCUITS. FINAL CONNECTION TO FURNITURE SYSTEM SHALL BE COORDINATED WITH FURNITURE SYSTEM INSTALLER. FURNITURE SYSTEM FEED SHALL BE A 2+2, 8-WIRE SYSTEM CONSISTING OF 4#12 HOT \(H\), 2#12 NEUTRAL \(N\), &amp; 2#12 EQUIPMENT GROUND \(EG\) IN 3/4" CONDUIT. PROVIDE LEGRAND WIREMOLD 4" FIRE RATED FURNITURE FEED POKE-THRU DEVICE WITH 3/4"C FOR POWER, 44FATC15 OR EQUIVALENT. VERIFY WITH FURNITURE VENDOR AND ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ORDERING AND ROUGH-IN. CONFIRM FINISH WITH ARCHITECT AND DATA REQUIREMENTS WITH IT DRAWINGS. REFER TO ELECTRICAL DETAIL SHEET FOR TYPICAL FURNITURE SYSTEM LAYOUT AND FURNITURE FEED. VERIFY EQUIPMENT POWER CONNECTIONS WITH ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ORDERING/ROUGH-IN. ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR SHALL COORDINATE WITH FIRE ALARM SYSTEM TO SHUT DOWN AV SOUND SYSTEM WITH ASSOCIATED OUTLETS IN ENCLOSED ROOMS WHEN FIRE ALARM SYSTEM IS ACTIVATED, AS REQUIRED. AV CONTRACTOR TO PROVIDE RELAY INTEGRATED POWER DISTRIBUTION DEVICE FURMAN CN-15MP MINIPORT OR EQUIVALENT.  PROVIDE 6" POKE-THROUGH DEVICE LEGRAND WIREMOLD 6AT OR EQUIVALENT TO SERVE POWER AND DATA. REFER TO AV/IT PLANS FOR FURTHER AV EQUIPMENT SPECIFICATIONS. VERIFY WITH ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ORDERING/ROUGH-IN. PROVIDE 8" POKE-THROUGH DEVICE LEGRAND WIREMOLD 8AT OR EQUIVALENT TO SERVE POWER, DATA AND HDMI. REFER TO AV/IT PLANS FOR FURTHER AV EQUIPMENT SPECIFICATIONS. VERIFY WITH ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ORDERING/ROUGH-IN. PROVIDE 1" CONDUIT ONLY WITH PULL WIRE AND REQUIRED BACK BOX STUB UP TO CEILING SPACE OR PLENUM FOR CARD READER. COORDINATE WITH SECURITY AND/OR AV/IT CONSULTANT PRIOR TO ROUGH-IN. REFER TO AV/IT DRAWINGS FOR ALL REQUIRED CARD READER LOCATIONS. PROVIDE 120V CIRCUIT FOR ELEVATOR SMOKE CURTAIN, SMOKE GUARD SYSTEM MODEL   200400OR EQUIVALENT. PROVIDE CONTROL AS REQUIRED FOR WORKABLE SYSTEM. ALL 120 VOLT, SINGLE PHASE, 15-20 AMP RECEPTACLES INSTALLED WITHIN 6' OF ANY POINT ALONG THE OUTSIDE EDGE OF A SINK SHALL BE GFCI PROTECTED. FOR RECEPTACLES NOT ACCESSIBLE, GFCI CIRCUIT BREAKER TO BE PROVIDED. NOT USED. NOT USED. VERIFY ROOM POWER REQUIREMENTS WITH AV/IT CONSULTANT PRIOR TO ROUGH-IN. PROVIDE AND INSTALL RATED DISCONNECT SWITCH AND AS REQUIRED FOR CONNECTIONS TO ELECTRIC WATER HEATER LOCATED PER PLUMBING DRAWINGS. LOCATE AND INSTALL DISCONNECT SWITCH ADJACENT TO ELECTRIC WATER HEATER AND COORDINATE EXACT REQUIREMENTS TO PLUMBING CONTRACTOR BEFORE ROUGH-IN. 120V RECEPTACLES IN OFFICES, LOBBIES, CONFERENCE ROOMS, PANTRIES, AND COPY ROOMS SHALL BE CONTROLLED AND AUTOMATICALLY TURN OFF WITH THE LIGHTS PER TITLE 24. A CONTROLLED RECEPTACLE DISTINCTLY LABELED SHALL BE LOCATED WITHIN 6' OF EACH UNCONTROLLED RECEPTACLE. PROVIDE SPLIT CIRCUITING RECEPTACLES, HALF CONTROLLED AND HALF UNCONTROLLED, WHERE REQUIRED. ROUTE EACH CONTROLLED RECEPTACLE CIRCUIT THROUGH A RELAY. TIE RELAY TO LOCAL CONTROL UNIT AND OCCUPANCY SENSOR. REFER TO WIRING DIAGRAM ON SHEET E032. FURROUT WALL 6" TO ALLOW FOR RECESSED INSTALLATION OF PANEL. CONFIRM AND COORDINATE FINAL PANEL INSTALL LOCATION WITH ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ORDERING/ROUGH-IN. PROVIDE HARDWIRED CONNECTION TO ALL PHONE BOOTHS. VERIFY WITH ARCHITECT AND FURNITURE VENDOR THE PHONE BOOTH POWER REQUIREMENTS PRIOR TO ORDERING AND ROUGH-IN. PER AV DRAWINGS, PROVIDE 1-1/4" CONDUIT TO NEAREST ACCESSIBLE CEILING FOR AV, 1" CONDUIT TO NEAREST ACCESSIBLE CEILING FOR DATA. REFER TO AV DRAWINGS FOR FURTHER INFORMATION AND EXACT REQUIREMENTS. PROVIDE 4" POKE-THROUGH DEVICE LEGRAND WIREMOLD 4AT OR EQUIVALENT TO SERVE POWER. VERIFY WITH ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ORDERING/ROUGH-IN. PROVIDE LEGRAND CONNECTRAC EXPRESS KIT FOR 1-CIRCUIT POWER CONNECTION TO SERVE EQUIPMENT. VERIFY WITH ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ORDERING/ROUGH-IN. COORDINATE ALL CONNECTIONS WITH FURNITURE VENDOR PRIOR TO ORDERING/ROUGH-IN.</p></body>)>>
endobj
