2664 0 obj<</Border[0 0 0]/Contents(1. DRAWING SHOWS DESIRED ELECTRICAL LAYOUT WITH NEW LOCATION OF RECEPTACLES, HARD WIRED DRAWING SHOWS DESIRED ELECTRICAL LAYOUT WITH NEW LOCATION OF RECEPTACLES, HARD WIRED JUNCTION BOXES, CONDUIT AND CIRCUITING REQUIREMENTS. CONTRACTOR SHALL COORDINATE FINAL LOCATION OF DEVICES WITH OTHER SUBCONTRACTOR TO AVOID CONFLICT OF ACCESS TO THE DEVICES.  2. ALL JUNCTION BOXES SHALL BE SIZED PER NEC TABLE 314-16\(A\). ALL JUNCTION BOXES SHALL BE SIZED PER NEC TABLE 314-16\(A\). 3. ALL PENETRATIONS INTO FIRE RATED WALL AND ALL FLOOR CORING SHALL BE FIRE SEALED ALL PENETRATIONS INTO FIRE RATED WALL AND ALL FLOOR CORING SHALL BE FIRE SEALED X-RAYED FOR CORING. FOR ALL CONDUIT PENETRATION, SEE TYPICAL DETAIL ON ARCHITECTURAL DRAWINGS. 4. UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED, ALL MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT REQUIRING ELECTRICAL CONNECTION\(S\) ARE UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED, ALL MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT REQUIRING ELECTRICAL CONNECTION\(S\) ARE NEW. SEE MECHANICAL DRAWINGS FOR ACTUAL LOCATION AND ELECTRICAL REQUIREMENTS FOR ALL MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT. 5. NO EQUIPMENT, JUNCTION BOX, ETC. REQUIRING ACCESS SHALL BE LOCATED IN HARD CEILING NO EQUIPMENT, JUNCTION BOX, ETC. REQUIRING ACCESS SHALL BE LOCATED IN HARD CEILING AREAS \(UNLESS ACCESS PANEL IS PROVIDED, COORDINATE WITH ARCHITECT\). RELOCATE ANY EXISTING EQUIPMENT, JUNCTION BOX, ETC. TO ACCESSIBLE CEILING AREA. 6. ALL EXPOSED CONDUITS SHALL BE EMT AND RUN AT 90 DEGREE ANGLES AND PARALLEL TO ALL EXPOSED CONDUITS SHALL BE EMT AND RUN AT 90 DEGREE ANGLES AND PARALLEL TO BUILDING STRUCTURE. TELE/DATA CONDUITS AND POWER CONDUITS IF RUN PARALLEL, SHALL HAVE NO LESS THAN 12" SEPARATION. 7. FLEX CONDUIT IS NOT ALLOWED TO BE VISIBLE. FLEX CONDUIT IS NOT ALLOWED TO BE VISIBLE. 8. PROVIDE AUDIO/VIDEO SYSTEM CONDUITS AND DEVICE BACK BOXES AS PER AUDIO/VISUAL PROVIDE AUDIO/VIDEO SYSTEM CONDUITS AND DEVICE BACK BOXES AS PER AUDIO/VISUAL CONSULTANT DRAWINGS. 9. FOR EQUIPMENT REQUIRING SPECIAL RECEPTACLE, PROVIDE RECEPTACLE WITH NEMA CONFIGURATION FOR EQUIPMENT REQUIRING SPECIAL RECEPTACLE, PROVIDE RECEPTACLE WITH NEMA CONFIGURATION TO MATCH EQUIPMENT PLUG. VERIFY WITH EQUIPMENT MANUFACTURER. 10. PROVIDE 3/4" CONDUIT FROM EACH THERMOSTAT TO RESPECTIVE AC UNIT OR EXHAUST FAN. REFER PROVIDE 3/4" CONDUIT FROM EACH THERMOSTAT TO RESPECTIVE AC UNIT OR EXHAUST FAN. REFER TO MECHANICAL DRAWINGS EXACT LOCATIONS AND REQUIREMENTS. 11. FOR EXACT LOCATION OF MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT, REFER TO HVAC AND PLUMBING PLANS.  FOR EXACT LOCATION OF MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT, REFER TO HVAC AND PLUMBING PLANS.  12. CONTRACTOR SHALL VERIFY AND COORDINATE WITH ARCHITECTURAL DRAWINGS AND ELEVATIONS AND CONTRACTOR SHALL VERIFY AND COORDINATE WITH ARCHITECTURAL DRAWINGS AND ELEVATIONS AND OTHER CONSULTANTS DRAWING LOCATION AND ELEVATION OF ALL RECEPTACLES, CONNECTIONS AND DEVICES PRIOR TO ROUGH-IN AND INSTALLATIONS. 13. WHERE INDICATED ON HVAC PLANS AS PART OF ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR'S WORK AND NOT WHERE INDICATED ON HVAC PLANS AS PART OF ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR'S WORK AND NOT COVERED ON THIS PLAN. PROVIDE CONDUIT AND CONTROL WIRING \(IF LOW VOLTAGE, PROVIDE CONTROL TRANSFORMER\) AS REQUIRED. 14. REFER TO SECURITY SYSTEM CONSULTANT'S DRAWINGS FOR SECURITY DEVICE LOCATIONS AND FOR REFER TO SECURITY SYSTEM CONSULTANT'S DRAWINGS FOR SECURITY DEVICE LOCATIONS AND FOR OTHER SECURITY SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS AND PROVIDE AS REQUIRED BACKBOX, CONDUIT AND WIRES FOR COMPLETE AND WORKABLE INSTALLATIONS. SEE ALSO SECURITY DRAWINGS FOR MORE INFORMATION. 15. REFER TO AV SYSTEM CONSULTANT'S DRAWINGS FOR AV DEVICE WITH REQUIRED BACKBOX, CONDUIT, REFER TO AV SYSTEM CONSULTANT'S DRAWINGS FOR AV DEVICE WITH REQUIRED BACKBOX, CONDUIT, PULL WIRES AND EQUIPMENT LOCATIONS AND FOR OTHER AV SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS. PROVIDE ISOLATED GROUND TYPE RECEPTACLE WHERE SUCH OUTLETS ARE UTILIZED TO SERVE AV SYSTEM EQUIPMENT.  16. ALL RECEPTACLES INSTALLED TO SERVE COUNTERTOP SURFACES WITH SINK SHALL BE GFI TYPE ALL RECEPTACLES INSTALLED TO SERVE COUNTERTOP SURFACES WITH SINK SHALL BE GFI TYPE RECEPTACLES. 17. ALL 2-CIRCUIT HOME RUNS SHARING NEUTRAL SHALL BE PROVIDED WITH #10 NEUTRAL WIRES. ALL 2-CIRCUIT HOME RUNS SHARING NEUTRAL SHALL BE PROVIDED WITH #10 NEUTRAL WIRES. 18. PROVIDE AND INSTALL #10 WIRES FOR 120V CIRCUIT HOMERUNS MORE THAN 100'-0". PROVIDE AND INSTALL #10 WIRES FOR 120V CIRCUIT HOMERUNS MORE THAN 100'-0". 19. PROVIDE PERMANENT LABEL TO EACH RECEPTACLE ON THIS POWER PLAN, SHOWING PANEL NAME PROVIDE PERMANENT LABEL TO EACH RECEPTACLE ON THIS POWER PLAN, SHOWING PANEL NAME AND CIRCUIT NUMBER USED FOR POWER SOURCE. 20. PROVIDE 2/3-POLE CIRCUIT BREAKERS OR PROVIDE HANDLE TIE TO CIRCUIT BREAKERS SHARING PROVIDE 2/3-POLE CIRCUIT BREAKERS OR PROVIDE HANDLE TIE TO CIRCUIT BREAKERS SHARING THE SAME NEUTRAL PER NEC 2020/CEC 2022. 21. GFCI/GFI PROTECTED RECEPTACLE OUTLETS SHALL BE INSTALLED IN A READILY ACCESSIBLE GFCI/GFI PROTECTED RECEPTACLE OUTLETS SHALL BE INSTALLED IN A READILY ACCESSIBLE LOCATION OR PROVIDE GFCI CIRCUIT BREAKER\(S\). 22. PROVIDE LOCK-ON CIRCUIT BREAKER TO CIRCUIT AS THAT FEEDS SECURITY AND FIRE ALARM PANEL. PROVIDE LOCK-ON CIRCUIT BREAKER TO CIRCUIT AS THAT FEEDS SECURITY AND FIRE ALARM PANEL. 23. PROVIDE SEPARATE NEUTRAL TO 120V, DEDICATED CIRCUIT PER NEC 2020/CEC 2022. PROVIDE SEPARATE NEUTRAL TO 120V, DEDICATED CIRCUIT PER NEC 2020/CEC 2022. 24. GYP CEILING AREAS SHALL BE KEPT FREE OF ACCESS PANELS. THIS WILL REQUIRE THE LOCATION GYP CEILING AREAS SHALL BE KEPT FREE OF ACCESS PANELS. THIS WILL REQUIRE THE LOCATION OF ALL NEW EQUIPMENT REQUIRING ACCESS AWAY FROM THE GYP CEILING AREAS SUCH AS J-BOXES, ETC. 25. ALL FLOOR FEEDS SHALL HAVE FULL EMT CONDUIT FROM UNDER SIDE OF FLOOR RETURNING TO ALL FLOOR FEEDS SHALL HAVE FULL EMT CONDUIT FROM UNDER SIDE OF FLOOR RETURNING TO NEAREST FULL HEIGHT WALL AND INTO SPACE. OPEN WIRING IS NOT ALLOWED. 26. RUN SEPARATE GROUND AND NEUTRAL FOR ALL A/V AND IT RECEPTACLES.RUN SEPARATE GROUND AND NEUTRAL FOR ALL A/V AND IT RECEPTACLES.)/F 64/Rect[98 347 656 749]/Subtype/Square/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/NM(XDUHPAIOVVCYALZF)/M(D:20260811142352-07'00')/AP<</N 1845 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>1. DRAWING SHOWS DESIRED ELECTRICAL LAYOUT WITH NEW LOCATION OF RECEPTACLES, HARD WIRED DRAWING SHOWS DESIRED ELECTRICAL LAYOUT WITH NEW LOCATION OF RECEPTACLES, HARD WIRED JUNCTION BOXES, CONDUIT AND CIRCUITING REQUIREMENTS. CONTRACTOR SHALL COORDINATE FINAL LOCATION OF DEVICES WITH OTHER SUBCONTRACTOR TO AVOID CONFLICT OF ACCESS TO THE DEVICES.  2. ALL JUNCTION BOXES SHALL BE SIZED PER NEC TABLE 314-16\(A\). ALL JUNCTION BOXES SHALL BE SIZED PER NEC TABLE 314-16\(A\). 3. ALL PENETRATIONS INTO FIRE RATED WALL AND ALL FLOOR CORING SHALL BE FIRE SEALED ALL PENETRATIONS INTO FIRE RATED WALL AND ALL FLOOR CORING SHALL BE FIRE SEALED X-RAYED FOR CORING. FOR ALL CONDUIT PENETRATION, SEE TYPICAL DETAIL ON ARCHITECTURAL DRAWINGS. 4. UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED, ALL MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT REQUIRING ELECTRICAL CONNECTION\(S\) ARE UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED, ALL MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT REQUIRING ELECTRICAL CONNECTION\(S\) ARE NEW. SEE MECHANICAL DRAWINGS FOR ACTUAL LOCATION AND ELECTRICAL REQUIREMENTS FOR ALL MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT. 5. NO EQUIPMENT, JUNCTION BOX, ETC. REQUIRING ACCESS SHALL BE LOCATED IN HARD CEILING NO EQUIPMENT, JUNCTION BOX, ETC. REQUIRING ACCESS SHALL BE LOCATED IN HARD CEILING AREAS \(UNLESS ACCESS PANEL IS PROVIDED, COORDINATE WITH ARCHITECT\). RELOCATE ANY EXISTING EQUIPMENT, JUNCTION BOX, ETC. TO ACCESSIBLE CEILING AREA. 6. ALL EXPOSED CONDUITS SHALL BE EMT AND RUN AT 90 DEGREE ANGLES AND PARALLEL TO ALL EXPOSED CONDUITS SHALL BE EMT AND RUN AT 90 DEGREE ANGLES AND PARALLEL TO BUILDING STRUCTURE. TELE/DATA CONDUITS AND POWER CONDUITS IF RUN PARALLEL, SHALL HAVE NO LESS THAN 12" SEPARATION. 7. FLEX CONDUIT IS NOT ALLOWED TO BE VISIBLE. FLEX CONDUIT IS NOT ALLOWED TO BE VISIBLE. 8. PROVIDE AUDIO/VIDEO SYSTEM CONDUITS AND DEVICE BACK BOXES AS PER AUDIO/VISUAL PROVIDE AUDIO/VIDEO SYSTEM CONDUITS AND DEVICE BACK BOXES AS PER AUDIO/VISUAL CONSULTANT DRAWINGS. 9. FOR EQUIPMENT REQUIRING SPECIAL RECEPTACLE, PROVIDE RECEPTACLE WITH NEMA CONFIGURATION FOR EQUIPMENT REQUIRING SPECIAL RECEPTACLE, PROVIDE RECEPTACLE WITH NEMA CONFIGURATION TO MATCH EQUIPMENT PLUG. VERIFY WITH EQUIPMENT MANUFACTURER. 10. PROVIDE 3/4" CONDUIT FROM EACH THERMOSTAT TO RESPECTIVE AC UNIT OR EXHAUST FAN. REFER PROVIDE 3/4" CONDUIT FROM EACH THERMOSTAT TO RESPECTIVE AC UNIT OR EXHAUST FAN. REFER TO MECHANICAL DRAWINGS EXACT LOCATIONS AND REQUIREMENTS. 11. FOR EXACT LOCATION OF MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT, REFER TO HVAC AND PLUMBING PLANS.  FOR EXACT LOCATION OF MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT, REFER TO HVAC AND PLUMBING PLANS.  12. CONTRACTOR SHALL VERIFY AND COORDINATE WITH ARCHITECTURAL DRAWINGS AND ELEVATIONS AND CONTRACTOR SHALL VERIFY AND COORDINATE WITH ARCHITECTURAL DRAWINGS AND ELEVATIONS AND OTHER CONSULTANTS DRAWING LOCATION AND ELEVATION OF ALL RECEPTACLES, CONNECTIONS AND DEVICES PRIOR TO ROUGH-IN AND INSTALLATIONS. 13. WHERE INDICATED ON HVAC PLANS AS PART OF ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR'S WORK AND NOT WHERE INDICATED ON HVAC PLANS AS PART OF ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR'S WORK AND NOT COVERED ON THIS PLAN. PROVIDE CONDUIT AND CONTROL WIRING \(IF LOW VOLTAGE, PROVIDE CONTROL TRANSFORMER\) AS REQUIRED. 14. REFER TO SECURITY SYSTEM CONSULTANT'S DRAWINGS FOR SECURITY DEVICE LOCATIONS AND FOR REFER TO SECURITY SYSTEM CONSULTANT'S DRAWINGS FOR SECURITY DEVICE LOCATIONS AND FOR OTHER SECURITY SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS AND PROVIDE AS REQUIRED BACKBOX, CONDUIT AND WIRES FOR COMPLETE AND WORKABLE INSTALLATIONS. SEE ALSO SECURITY DRAWINGS FOR MORE INFORMATION. 15. REFER TO AV SYSTEM CONSULTANT'S DRAWINGS FOR AV DEVICE WITH REQUIRED BACKBOX, CONDUIT, REFER TO AV SYSTEM CONSULTANT'S DRAWINGS FOR AV DEVICE WITH REQUIRED BACKBOX, CONDUIT, PULL WIRES AND EQUIPMENT LOCATIONS AND FOR OTHER AV SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS. PROVIDE ISOLATED GROUND TYPE RECEPTACLE WHERE SUCH OUTLETS ARE UTILIZED TO SERVE AV SYSTEM EQUIPMENT.  16. ALL RECEPTACLES INSTALLED TO SERVE COUNTERTOP SURFACES WITH SINK SHALL BE GFI TYPE ALL RECEPTACLES INSTALLED TO SERVE COUNTERTOP SURFACES WITH SINK SHALL BE GFI TYPE RECEPTACLES. 17. ALL 2-CIRCUIT HOME RUNS SHARING NEUTRAL SHALL BE PROVIDED WITH #10 NEUTRAL WIRES. ALL 2-CIRCUIT HOME RUNS SHARING NEUTRAL SHALL BE PROVIDED WITH #10 NEUTRAL WIRES. 18. PROVIDE AND INSTALL #10 WIRES FOR 120V CIRCUIT HOMERUNS MORE THAN 100'-0". PROVIDE AND INSTALL #10 WIRES FOR 120V CIRCUIT HOMERUNS MORE THAN 100'-0". 19. PROVIDE PERMANENT LABEL TO EACH RECEPTACLE ON THIS POWER PLAN, SHOWING PANEL NAME PROVIDE PERMANENT LABEL TO EACH RECEPTACLE ON THIS POWER PLAN, SHOWING PANEL NAME AND CIRCUIT NUMBER USED FOR POWER SOURCE. 20. PROVIDE 2/3-POLE CIRCUIT BREAKERS OR PROVIDE HANDLE TIE TO CIRCUIT BREAKERS SHARING PROVIDE 2/3-POLE CIRCUIT BREAKERS OR PROVIDE HANDLE TIE TO CIRCUIT BREAKERS SHARING THE SAME NEUTRAL PER NEC 2020/CEC 2022. 21. GFCI/GFI PROTECTED RECEPTACLE OUTLETS SHALL BE INSTALLED IN A READILY ACCESSIBLE GFCI/GFI PROTECTED RECEPTACLE OUTLETS SHALL BE INSTALLED IN A READILY ACCESSIBLE LOCATION OR PROVIDE GFCI CIRCUIT BREAKER\(S\). 22. PROVIDE LOCK-ON CIRCUIT BREAKER TO CIRCUIT AS THAT FEEDS SECURITY AND FIRE ALARM PANEL. PROVIDE LOCK-ON CIRCUIT BREAKER TO CIRCUIT AS THAT FEEDS SECURITY AND FIRE ALARM PANEL. 23. PROVIDE SEPARATE NEUTRAL TO 120V, DEDICATED CIRCUIT PER NEC 2020/CEC 2022. PROVIDE SEPARATE NEUTRAL TO 120V, DEDICATED CIRCUIT PER NEC 2020/CEC 2022. 24. GYP CEILING AREAS SHALL BE KEPT FREE OF ACCESS PANELS. THIS WILL REQUIRE THE LOCATION GYP CEILING AREAS SHALL BE KEPT FREE OF ACCESS PANELS. THIS WILL REQUIRE THE LOCATION OF ALL NEW EQUIPMENT REQUIRING ACCESS AWAY FROM THE GYP CEILING AREAS SUCH AS J-BOXES, ETC. 25. ALL FLOOR FEEDS SHALL HAVE FULL EMT CONDUIT FROM UNDER SIDE OF FLOOR RETURNING TO ALL FLOOR FEEDS SHALL HAVE FULL EMT CONDUIT FROM UNDER SIDE OF FLOOR 