7609 0 obj<</Border[0 0 0]/Contents(1. NO EQUIPMENT JUNCTION BOXES, ETC. REQUIRING ACCESS SHALL BE LOCATED NO EQUIPMENT JUNCTION BOXES, ETC. REQUIRING ACCESS SHALL BE LOCATED IN HARD CEILING AREAS \(UNLESS ACCESS PANEL IS PROVIDED, COORDINATE WITH THE ARCHITECT\).  2. VERIFY THE TYPE OF CEILING SYSTEM WITH GENERAL CONTRACTOR OR CEILING VERIFY THE TYPE OF CEILING SYSTEM WITH GENERAL CONTRACTOR OR CEILING CONTRACTOR.  PROVIDE FIXTURES WHICH ARE COMPATIBLE WITH THE CEILING SYSTEM AND INCLUDE ALL REQUIRED MOUNTING ACCESSORIES AND HARDWARE. 3. SUPPORT CEILING MOUNTED LIGHTING FIXTURES DIRECTLY FROM THE BUILDING SUPPORT CEILING MOUNTED LIGHTING FIXTURES DIRECTLY FROM THE BUILDING STRUCTURE. DO NOT SUPPORT FIXTURES FROM PIPING, DUCTWORK OR ANY OTHER EQUIPMENT, OR SOLELY FROM THE SUSPENDED CEILING. 4. WHERE MULTIPLE SWITCHES ARE INDICATED, SWITCHES SHALL BE GANGED WHERE MULTIPLE SWITCHES ARE INDICATED, SWITCHES SHALL BE GANGED UNDER A COMMON WALL PLATE. 5. ALL SWITCH LOCATIONS SHALL BE VERIFIED WITH THE ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ALL SWITCH LOCATIONS SHALL BE VERIFIED WITH THE ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ROUGH IN.  6. ALL EXPOSED CONDUITS SHALL BE EMT AND SHALL BE RUN 90 DEGREES ALL EXPOSED CONDUITS SHALL BE EMT AND SHALL BE RUN 90 DEGREES PERPENDICULAR AND PARALLEL TO CEILING STRUCTURE AND HUG TO UNDERSIDE OF SLAB.   7. CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE ADDITIONAL EXIT SIGN\(S\) IF REQUIRED BY THE CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE ADDITIONAL EXIT SIGN\(S\) IF REQUIRED BY THE CITY FIRE MARSHALL INSPECTOR AT NO ADDITIONAL COST TO THE OWNER. 8. CONTRACTOR SHALL VERIFY VOLTAGES FOR ALL FIXTURES PRIOR TO ORDERING.   CONTRACTOR SHALL VERIFY VOLTAGES FOR ALL FIXTURES PRIOR TO ORDERING.   9. ALL PENDANT FIXTURES SHALL BE PROVIDED WITH SUFFICIENT STEM OR ALL PENDANT FIXTURES SHALL BE PROVIDED WITH SUFFICIENT STEM OR SUSPENSION CABLE LENGTH PRIOR TO INSTALLATION. VERIFY LENGTHS WITH ARCHITECT. 10. CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE ALL NECESSARY HARDWARE, ELECTRICAL CABLE, CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE ALL NECESSARY HARDWARE, ELECTRICAL CABLE, TIMERS, TRANSFORMERS, ETC., AS REQUIRED FOR COMPLETION OF INSTALLATION. WHERE LOW VOLTAGE FIXTURES ARE NOT EQUIPPED WITH STEP DOWN TRANSFORMER, PROVIDE TRANSFORMER OF REQUIRED SIZE AND RATING TO ACCOMMODATE CONNECTED LIGHTING LOAD. 11. ANY FIXTURE SUBSTITUTION MUST BE APPROVED BY THE ARCHITECT AND/OR ANY FIXTURE SUBSTITUTION MUST BE APPROVED BY THE ARCHITECT AND/OR LIGHTING DESIGNER PRIOR TO BID. CONTRACTOR MUST BE PREPARED TO SUPPLY A SAMPLE AND/OR PHOTOMETRIC DATA IF REQUIRED. IF SUBSTITUTION IS REJECTED, CONTRACTOR MUST BE PREPARED TO PROVIDE SPECIFIED PRODUCT WITHOUT DELAY. 12. DRAWING SHOWS CIRCUITING AND SWITCHING REQUIREMENTS AND FIXTURE TYPES DRAWING SHOWS CIRCUITING AND SWITCHING REQUIREMENTS AND FIXTURE TYPES ONLY, VERIFY EXACT LIGHTING FIXTURES AND STANDARD SWITCHING WITH ARCHITECT AND OWNER PRIOR TO INSTALLATION. ALSO VERIFY EXACT LIGHTING FIXTURES VOLTAGE AND FINISH PRIOR TO INSTALLATION.   13. PROVIDE AND INSTALL #10 WIRES FOR 120V CIRCUIT HOME RUNS MORE THAN PROVIDE AND INSTALL #10 WIRES FOR 120V CIRCUIT HOME RUNS MORE THAN 100'-0".  14. PROVIDE UNISTRUT CHANNEL SUPPORT AND BRACKETS FOR MOUNTING OF PROVIDE UNISTRUT CHANNEL SUPPORT AND BRACKETS FOR MOUNTING OF J-BOX FOR SIGN WHERE NO STRUCTURE OR OTHER MEANS OF MOUNTING THE DEVICES CURRENTLY EXIST.   15. ALL FIXTURES THAT HAVE A LABEL SHOWING CIRCUIT NUMBER AND A SWITCH ALL FIXTURES THAT HAVE A LABEL SHOWING CIRCUIT NUMBER AND A SWITCH LEG SHOW WHICH RELAY IT IS CONNECTED TO. FOR DAYLIGHT CONTROLS THE SWITCH LEG IS FOLLOWED BY X NUMBER OF "+" SIGNS. THE "+" SIGNS INDICATE THAT THE FIXTURE THAT IS ON THE SAME SWITCH LEG IS CONNECTED TO SEPARATE DIMMERS OF THE ROOM CONTROLLER PER WIRING DIAGRAM. SEE DETAIL SHEET E0.32. A GENERIC EXAMPLE MAY BE: LABELS "1A" "1A+" AND "1A++" SIGNIFY THAT THE FIXTURE IS TIED TO CIRCUIT 1. "A" SIGNIFIES IT IS ON RELAY X, MANUAL DIMMING. "A+" SIGNIFIES THAT IT IS ON RELAY X, SECONDARY DAYLIGHT ZONE. "A++" SIGNIFIES THAT IT IS ON RELAY X, PRIMARY DAYLIGHT ZONE.   16. EXIT SIGNS LOCATIONS SHALL BE COORDINATED AND APPROVED BY FIRE EXIT SIGNS LOCATIONS SHALL BE COORDINATED AND APPROVED BY FIRE MARSHALL. 17. PROVIDE ADDITIONAL EXIT SIGN PRE FIRE MARSHALL REQUEST. \(TYPICAL ALL PROVIDE ADDITIONAL EXIT SIGN PRE FIRE MARSHALL REQUEST. \(TYPICAL ALL LIGHTING PLANS\). 18. EMERGENCY LIGHTING CIRCUITS SHALL BE IN A SEPARATE RACEWAY FROM EMERGENCY LIGHTING CIRCUITS SHALL BE IN A SEPARATE RACEWAY FROM NORMAL LIGHTING CIRCUITS. 19. CONTRACTOR TO CONFIRM WINDOW HEAD HEIGHT AND SEPARATION OF PRIMARY CONTRACTOR TO CONFIRM WINDOW HEAD HEIGHT AND SEPARATION OF PRIMARY AND SECONDARY DAYLIT ZONES. 20. CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE AND INSTALL LIGHTING DEMAND AND RESPONSE CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE AND INSTALL LIGHTING DEMAND AND RESPONSE SYSTEM PER CALIFORNIA ENERGY CODE 2022 SECTION 110.12\(C\). CONTRACTOR SHALL CONFIGURE THE LIGHTING SYSTEM TO ACHIEVE MINIMUM OF 15% BELOW THE TOTAL INSTALLED LIGHTING POWER. 21. ANY DEVICES CONTROLLER EMERGENCY CIRCUITS/FIXTURES TO HAVE UL 924 ANY DEVICES CONTROLLER EMERGENCY CIRCUITS/FIXTURES TO HAVE UL 924 CERTIFICATION OR AHJ APPROVED EQUIVALENT.)/F 64/Rect[556 334 1377 740]/Subtype/Square/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/NM(NPPPMHHOKBJAWDGA)/M(D:20260811143629-07'00')/AP<</N 6749 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>1. NO EQUIPMENT JUNCTION BOXES, ETC. REQUIRING ACCESS SHALL BE LOCATED NO EQUIPMENT JUNCTION BOXES, ETC. REQUIRING ACCESS SHALL BE LOCATED IN HARD CEILING AREAS \(UNLESS ACCESS PANEL IS PROVIDED, COORDINATE WITH THE ARCHITECT\).  2. VERIFY THE TYPE OF CEILING SYSTEM WITH GENERAL CONTRACTOR OR CEILING VERIFY THE TYPE OF CEILING SYSTEM WITH GENERAL CONTRACTOR OR CEILING CONTRACTOR.  PROVIDE FIXTURES WHICH ARE COMPATIBLE WITH THE CEILING SYSTEM AND INCLUDE ALL REQUIRED MOUNTING ACCESSORIES AND HARDWARE. 3. SUPPORT CEILING MOUNTED LIGHTING FIXTURES DIRECTLY FROM THE BUILDING SUPPORT CEILING MOUNTED LIGHTING FIXTURES DIRECTLY FROM THE BUILDING STRUCTURE. DO NOT SUPPORT FIXTURES FROM PIPING, DUCTWORK OR ANY OTHER EQUIPMENT, OR SOLELY FROM THE SUSPENDED CEILING. 4. WHERE MULTIPLE SWITCHES ARE INDICATED, SWITCHES SHALL BE GANGED WHERE MULTIPLE SWITCHES ARE INDICATED, SWITCHES SHALL BE GANGED UNDER A COMMON WALL PLATE. 5. ALL SWITCH LOCATIONS SHALL BE VERIFIED WITH THE ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ALL SWITCH LOCATIONS SHALL BE VERIFIED WITH THE ARCHITECT PRIOR TO ROUGH IN.  6. ALL EXPOSED CONDUITS SHALL BE EMT AND SHALL BE RUN 90 DEGREES ALL EXPOSED CONDUITS SHALL BE EMT AND SHALL BE RUN 90 DEGREES PERPENDICULAR AND PARALLEL TO CEILING STRUCTURE AND HUG TO UNDERSIDE OF SLAB.   7. CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE ADDITIONAL EXIT SIGN\(S\) IF REQUIRED BY THE CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE ADDITIONAL EXIT SIGN\(S\) IF REQUIRED BY THE CITY FIRE MARSHALL INSPECTOR AT NO ADDITIONAL COST TO THE OWNER. 8. CONTRACTOR SHALL VERIFY VOLTAGES FOR ALL FIXTURES PRIOR TO ORDERING.   CONTRACTOR SHALL VERIFY VOLTAGES FOR ALL FIXTURES PRIOR TO ORDERING.   9. ALL PENDANT FIXTURES SHALL BE PROVIDED WITH SUFFICIENT STEM OR ALL PENDANT FIXTURES SHALL BE PROVIDED WITH SUFFICIENT STEM OR SUSPENSION CABLE LENGTH PRIOR TO INSTALLATION. VERIFY LENGTHS WITH ARCHITECT. 10. CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE ALL NECESSARY HARDWARE, ELECTRICAL CABLE, CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE ALL NECESSARY HARDWARE, ELECTRICAL CABLE, TIMERS, TRANSFORMERS, ETC., AS REQUIRED FOR COMPLETION OF INSTALLATION. WHERE LOW VOLTAGE FIXTURES ARE NOT EQUIPPED WITH STEP DOWN TRANSFORMER, PROVIDE TRANSFORMER OF REQUIRED SIZE AND RATING TO ACCOMMODATE CONNECTED LIGHTING LOAD. 11. ANY FIXTURE SUBSTITUTION MUST BE APPROVED BY THE ARCHITECT AND/OR ANY FIXTURE SUBSTITUTION MUST BE APPROVED BY THE ARCHITECT AND/OR LIGHTING DESIGNER PRIOR TO BID. CONTRACTOR MUST BE PREPARED TO SUPPLY A SAMPLE AND/OR PHOTOMETRIC DATA IF REQUIRED. IF SUBSTITUTION IS REJECTED, CONTRACTOR MUST BE PREPARED TO PROVIDE SPECIFIED PRODUCT WITHOUT DELAY. 12. DRAWING SHOWS CIRCUITING AND SWITCHING REQUIREMENTS AND FIXTURE TYPES DRAWING SHOWS CIRCUITING AND SWITCHING REQUIREMENTS AND FIXTURE TYPES ONLY, VERIFY EXACT LIGHTING FIXTURES AND STANDARD SWITCHING WITH ARCHITECT AND OWNER PRIOR TO INSTALLATION. ALSO VERIFY EXACT LIGHTING FIXTURES VOLTAGE AND FINISH PRIOR TO INSTALLATION.   13. PROVIDE AND INSTALL #10 WIRES FOR 120V CIRCUIT HOME RUNS MORE THAN PROVIDE AND INSTALL #10 WIRES FOR 120V CIRCUIT HOME RUNS MORE THAN 100'-0".  14. PROVIDE UNISTRUT CHANNEL SUPPORT AND BRACKETS FOR MOUNTING OF PROVIDE UNISTRUT CHANNEL SUPPORT AND BRACKETS FOR MOUNTING OF J-BOX FOR SIGN WHERE NO STRUCTURE OR OTHER MEANS OF MOUNTING THE DEVICES CURRENTLY EXIST.   15. ALL FIXTURES THAT HAVE A LABEL SHOWING CIRCUIT NUMBER AND A SWITCH ALL FIXTURES THAT HAVE A LABEL SHOWING CIRCUIT NUMBER AND A SWITCH LEG SHOW WHICH RELAY IT IS CONNECTED TO. FOR DAYLIGHT CONTROLS THE SWITCH LEG IS FOLLOWED BY X NUMBER OF "+" SIGNS. THE "+" SIGNS INDICATE THAT THE FIXTURE THAT IS ON THE SAME SWITCH LEG IS CONNECTED TO SEPARATE DIMMERS OF THE ROOM CONTROLLER PER WIRING DIAGRAM. SEE DETAIL SHEET E0.32. A GENERIC EXAMPLE MAY BE: LABELS "1A" "1A+" AND "1A++" SIGNIFY THAT THE FIXTURE IS TIED TO CIRCUIT 1. "A" SIGNIFIES IT IS ON RELAY X, MANUAL DIMMING. "A+" SIGNIFIES THAT IT IS ON RELAY X, SECONDARY DAYLIGHT ZONE. "A++" SIGNIFIES THAT IT IS ON RELAY X, PRIMARY DAYLIGHT ZONE.   16. EXIT SIGNS LOCATIONS SHALL BE COORDINATED AND APPROVED BY FIRE EXIT SIGNS LOCATIONS SHALL BE COORDINATED AND APPROVED BY FIRE MARSHALL. 17. PROVIDE ADDITIONAL EXIT SIGN PRE FIRE MARSHALL REQUEST. \(TYPICAL ALL PROVIDE ADDITIONAL EXIT SIGN PRE FIRE MARSHALL REQUEST. \(TYPICAL ALL LIGHTING PLANS\). 18. EMERGENCY LIGHTING CIRCUITS SHALL BE IN A SEPARATE RACEWAY FROM EMERGENCY LIGHTING CIRCUITS SHALL BE IN A SEPARATE RACEWAY FROM NORMAL LIGHTING CIRCUITS. 19. CONTRACTOR TO CONFIRM WINDOW HEAD HEIGHT AND SEPARATION OF PRIMARY CONTRACTOR TO CONFIRM WINDOW HEAD HEIGHT AND SEPARATION OF PRIMARY AND SECONDARY DAYLIT ZONES. 20. CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE AND INSTALL LIGHTING DEMAND AND RESPONSE CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE AND INSTALL LIGHTING DEMAND AND RESPONSE SYSTEM PER CALIFORNIA ENERGY CODE 2022 SECTION 110.12\(C\). CONTRACTOR SHALL CONFIGURE THE LIGHTING SYSTEM TO ACHIEVE MINIMUM OF 15% BELOW THE TOTAL INSTALLED LIGHTING POWER. 21. ANY DEVICES CONTROLLER EMERGENCY CIRCUITS/FIXTURES TO HAVE UL 924 ANY DEVICES CONTROLLER EMERGENCY CIRCUITS/FIXTURES TO HAVE UL 924 CERTIFICATION OR AHJ APPROVED EQUIVALENT.</p></body>)>>
