7658 0 obj<</Border[0 0 0]/Contents(ALL EXISTING LIGHTING FIXTURE AND THEIR CONTROLS IN THIS AREA NOT PART OF THIS SCOPE OF WORK ARE TO REMAIN. ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR TO MAINTAIN THE CONTINUITY OF EXISTING BRANCH CIRCUIT WIRING. ALL LIGHTING FIXTURES SHOWN WITH "/EM" AND SHADED ARE EMERGENCY. CONNECT ALL EMERGENCY LIGHTS TO EXISTING 277V EMERGENCY CIRCUIT ASSIGNED TO THIS FLOOR. ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR TO FIELD VERIFY EXACT CIRCUIT NUMBER. PROVIDE REQUIRED OCCUPANCY SENSORS, DAYLIGHT SENSORS, AND ADDITIONAL REQUIRED POWER PACKS THROUGHOUT. LOCATE SENSORS TO PROVIDE MAXIMUM COVERAGE PER MANUFACTURER'S RECOMMENDATIONS. FOR OCCUPANCY SENSORS IN PRIVATE OFFICES \(</=250SQFT\), CONFERENCE ROOMS AND MULTIPURPOSE ROOMS \(<1000SQFT\), THE OCCUPANCY SENSOR SHALL SERVE AS A PARTIAL-ON OCCUPANCY SENSOR \(LIGHTING POWER TURNS ON TO 50-70%\). REFER TO DETAIL SHEET E032 FOR FURTHER DETAILS.  PROVIDE WALL MOUNTED LOW VOLTAGE SCENE SELECTOR OR SLIDE DIMMER \(TYP.\). VERIFY EXACT LOCATION WITH THE ARCHITECT. PROVIDE A REMOTELY LOCATED ACCESSIBLE DRIVER TO POWER UNDERCABINET LIGHT FIXTURES. ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR SHALL VERIFY QUANTITIES WITH MANUFACTURER AND DETERMINE BEST LOCATIONS/PLACEMENTS FOR POWER SUPPLY/DRIVERS. NEW EXIT SIGNS SHALL BE \(2\) CIRCUIT FEED EXIT. CONNECT TO NEAREST EMERGENCY BRANCH CIRCUIT AND NEAREST NORMAL BRANCH CIRCUIT. SEE EXIT SIGN DETAIL ON THIS SHEET. ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR TO FIELD VERIFY ALL EXISTING CIRCUIT HOMERUNS SHOWN TO BE EXTENDED TO NEW LIGHT FIXTURES WITHIN THE SCOPE OF WORK. WHEN USING EXISTING CIRCUIT, ALL NEW RUNS OF FEEDERS MUST BE SIZED TO MATCH EXISTING FEEDERS. PROVIDE CURRENT LIMITER FOR TRACKLIGHTS. ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR TO DETERMINE BEST LOCATION/PLACEMENT FOR DEVICES.)/F 64/Rect[1421 330 1807 736]/Subtype/Square/T(AutoCAD SHX Text)/NM(UUMFTFEOKJOTDVQB)/M(D:20260811143629-07'00')/AP<</N 6798 0 R>>/RD[0 0 0 0]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:contentType="text/html" xfa:APIVersion="BluebeamPDFRevu:2018" xfa:spec="2.2.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p>ALL EXISTING LIGHTING FIXTURE AND THEIR CONTROLS IN THIS AREA NOT PART OF THIS SCOPE OF WORK ARE TO REMAIN. ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR TO MAINTAIN THE CONTINUITY OF EXISTING BRANCH CIRCUIT WIRING. ALL LIGHTING FIXTURES SHOWN WITH "/EM" AND SHADED ARE EMERGENCY. CONNECT ALL EMERGENCY LIGHTS TO EXISTING 277V EMERGENCY CIRCUIT ASSIGNED TO THIS FLOOR. ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR TO FIELD VERIFY EXACT CIRCUIT NUMBER. PROVIDE REQUIRED OCCUPANCY SENSORS, DAYLIGHT SENSORS, AND ADDITIONAL REQUIRED POWER PACKS THROUGHOUT. LOCATE SENSORS TO PROVIDE MAXIMUM COVERAGE PER MANUFACTURER'S RECOMMENDATIONS. FOR OCCUPANCY SENSORS IN PRIVATE OFFICES \(&lt;/=250SQFT\), CONFERENCE ROOMS AND MULTIPURPOSE ROOMS \(&lt;1000SQFT\), THE OCCUPANCY SENSOR SHALL SERVE AS A PARTIAL-ON OCCUPANCY SENSOR \(LIGHTING POWER TURNS ON TO 50-70%\). REFER TO DETAIL SHEET E032 FOR FURTHER DETAILS.  PROVIDE WALL MOUNTED LOW VOLTAGE SCENE SELECTOR OR SLIDE DIMMER \(TYP.\). VERIFY EXACT LOCATION WITH THE ARCHITECT. PROVIDE A REMOTELY LOCATED ACCESSIBLE DRIVER TO POWER UNDERCABINET LIGHT FIXTURES. ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR SHALL VERIFY QUANTITIES WITH MANUFACTURER AND DETERMINE BEST LOCATIONS/PLACEMENTS FOR POWER SUPPLY/DRIVERS. NEW EXIT SIGNS SHALL BE \(2\) CIRCUIT FEED EXIT. CONNECT TO NEAREST EMERGENCY BRANCH CIRCUIT AND NEAREST NORMAL BRANCH CIRCUIT. SEE EXIT SIGN DETAIL ON THIS SHEET. ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR TO FIELD VERIFY ALL EXISTING CIRCUIT HOMERUNS SHOWN TO BE EXTENDED TO NEW LIGHT FIXTURES WITHIN THE SCOPE OF WORK. WHEN USING EXISTING CIRCUIT, ALL NEW RUNS OF FEEDERS MUST BE SIZED TO MATCH EXISTING FEEDERS. PROVIDE CURRENT LIMITER FOR TRACKLIGHTS. ELECTRICAL CONTRACTOR TO DETERMINE BEST LOCATION/PLACEMENT FOR DEVICES.</p></body>)>>
endobj
