AND SEPARATION OF PRIMARY AND SECONDARY DAYLIT ZONES. 20. CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE AND INSTALL LIGHTING DEMAND AND RESPONSE CONTRACTOR SHALL PROVIDE AND INSTALL LIGHTING DEMAND AND RESPONSE SYSTEM PER CALIFORNIA ENERGY CODE 2022 SECTION 110.12\(C\). CONTRACTOR SHALL CONFIGURE THE LIGHTING SYSTEM TO ACHIEVE MINIMUM OF 15% BELOW THE TOTAL INSTALLED LIGHTING POWER. 21. ANY DEVICES CONTROLLER EMERGENCY CIRCUITS/FIXTURES TO HAVE UL 924 ANY DEVICES CONTROLLER EMERGENCY CIRCUITS/FIXTURES TO HAVE UL 924 CERTIFICATION OR AHJ APPROVED EQUIVALENT.</p></body>)>>
